  "text": "I put a chocolate long-sleeve top with a relaxed, sheer finish under a tailored chocolate blazer to soften your silhouette while keeping the look polished. The skirt you chose is silvery-grey plaid with a high waist and front slit—a perfect contrast to the dark brown of the tops, and it adds movement without breaking the autumn palette. I added a taupe feathered belt to cinch the waist where you want it marked, a burgundy pair of ballet flats that are comfortable yet elegant enough for coffee dates, and a soft pink beanie to keep you warm in the morning chill. A red structured bag with gold hardware brings a bold pop that matches your shoes without clashing, giving you something to carry essentials while still feeling effortless.",
  "how_to_wear": [
    "Leave the blazer unbuttoned for a relaxed, layered look, or button it just at the waistline if you want more structure during the morning yoga session.",
    "Tuck the feathered belt into the skirt’s high waist and let it drape naturally over the hips—it adds definition without tightening your shape.",
    "Keep the beanie on when stepping outside in the crisp autumn air, but take it off for your coffee date so your long hair can fall freely around your face."
